('127.54.d.7.C',3,'Scarification of a hard seed coat helps to:','["Allow water in so the seed can germinate", "Add nutrients", "Kill the seed", "Keep the seed dry"]'::jsonb,0,'Scratching the coat speeds germination.','original'),
('127.54.d.7.C',4,'Stratification involves exposing seeds to:','["Bright sun only", "Cold, moist conditions", "Constant heat", "Dry air"]'::jsonb,1,'Many seeds need a cold period to break dormancy.','original'),
('127.54.d.7.D',3,'A good soil-based growing medium should:','["Stay waterlogged", "Be pure clay only", "Drain well and hold some moisture", "Be pure sand with no nutrients"]'::jsonb,2,'Balance of drainage and retention matters.','original'),
('127.54.d.7.D',4,'Adding compost to garden soil mostly improves:','["Light levels", "Wind speed", "Sun angle", "Organic matter and structure"]'::jsonb,3,'Compost builds soil health.','original'),
('127.54.d.7.E',3,'Growing plants in water with nutrients and no soil is called:','["Hydroponics", "Xeriscaping", "Pruning", "Grafting"]'::jsonb,0,'Hydroponics uses nutrient solutions.','original'),
('127.54.d.7.E',4,'Perlite and vermiculite are used in:','["Pesticides", "Soilless media", "Mulch only", "Fertilizer sprays"]'::jsonb,1,'They lighten and aerate mixes.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.A',3,'Yellowing leaves with green veins can indicate:','["Over-pruning", "Too much light", "A nutrient deficiency such as iron", "A healthy plant"]'::jsonb,2,'Interveinal chlorosis often points to iron.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.A',4,'White powdery coating on leaves is a sign of:','["Frost", "Iron toxicity", "Sunscald", "Powdery mildew"]'::jsonb,3,'A fungal disease.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.B',3,'A weed is best described as:','["A plant growing where it is not wanted", "A rare flower", "A crop", "Any green plant"]'::jsonb,0,'Weeds compete with crops.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.B',4,'Mulch helps manage weeds by:','["Spreading seeds", "Blocking light to weed seeds", "Adding weeds", "Raising pH"]'::jsonb,1,'Mulch suppresses weed growth.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.C',3,'Integrated pest management combines:','["Ignoring pests", "Using only one pesticide", "Several methods to control pests with minimal chemicals", "Only spraying"]'::jsonb,2,'IPM uses monitoring, cultural, biological and chemical tools.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.C',4,'The first step in an IPM plan is usually:','["Ignoring thresholds", "Spraying everything", "Burning the crop", "Scouting and identifying the pest"]'::jsonb,3,'Know the pest before acting.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.D',3,'Cleaning pruning tools between plants helps to:','["Prevent spreading disease", "Add color", "Dull them", "Cool the plants"]'::jsonb,0,'Sanitation stops pathogens.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.D',4,'Removing fallen diseased leaves reduces:','["Water", "Sources of infection", "Light", "Plant height"]'::jsonb,1,'Debris harbors pathogens.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.E',3,'A pesticide applicator should always:','["Guess the amount", "Skip protection", "Follow the label directions", "Mix products at random"]'::jsonb,2,'The label is the law.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.E',4,'Pesticides should be stored:','["In soda bottles", "Open on a shelf", "Near food", "In original, labeled containers in a locked area"]'::jsonb,3,'Safe storage prevents accidents.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.F',3,'The signal word ''Danger'' on a pesticide label means the product is:','["Highly toxic or hazardous", "Harmless", "Organic", "Free"]'::jsonb,0,'Signal words show toxicity level.','original'),
('127.54.d.8.F',4,'The restricted-entry interval on a label tells you:','["The brand", "How long to stay out of a treated area", "The color", "The price"]'::jsonb,1,'REI protects workers.','original'),
('127.54.d.9.A',3,'In a dry climate, a landscaper would choose plants that are:','["Water loving", "Aquatic", "Drought tolerant", "Tropical only"]'::jsonb,2,'Plants must fit the conditions.','original'),
('127.54.d.9.A',4,'A slope that erodes easily is best planted with:','["Bare soil", "Annual flowers only", "Smooth gravel only", "Groundcovers with strong root systems"]'::jsonb,3,'Roots hold soil.','original'),
('127.54.d.9.B',3,'Evergreen shrubs are often chosen for landscapes to:','["Provide color and structure year-round", "Lose leaves", "Need no care", "Be seasonal only"]'::jsonb,0,'They keep foliage through winter.','original'),
('127.54.d.9.B',4,'Tulips are best planted as:','["Seeds in summer", "Bulbs in fall", "Grafts", "Cuttings"]'::jsonb,1,'Tulips are spring-flowering bulbs.','original'),
('127.54.d.9.C',3,'Unity in landscape design means:','["Random layout", "Every plant different", "All parts work together as one design", "No plan"]'::jsonb,2,'Unity gives a coherent look.','original'),
('127.54.d.9.C',4,'Repeating the same plant along a walkway adds:','["Disunity", "Chaos", "Weight", "Rhythm"]'::jsonb,3,'Repetition creates rhythm.','original'),
('127.54.d.9.D',3,'Planting native plants helps sustainability because they:','["Need less water and fertilizer", "Are invasive", "Need more water", "Are all imported"]'::jsonb,0,'Natives are adapted to local conditions.','original'),
('127.54.d.9.D',4,'Rain barrels are used to:','["Stop plant growth", "Collect water for later use", "Waste water", "Poison soil"]'::jsonb,1,'Water conservation saves resources.','original'),
