('127.55.d.4.C',4,'Energy-efficient greenhouses help growers by:','["Raising costs", "Reducing crops", "Using more fuel", "Lowering operating costs"]'::jsonb,3,'Savings improve profit.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.A',3,'A gutter-connected greenhouse has:','["Several bays joined along the sides", "No roof", "Only walls", "One tiny bay"]'::jsonb,0,'Gutter-connected houses share a roof line.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.A',4,'A benefit of polycarbonate panels over glass is that they:','["Block all light", "Are lighter and resist breakage", "Are heavier", "Break easily"]'::jsonb,1,'Polycarbonate is durable and insulating.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.B',3,'Polyethylene film is a common greenhouse covering because it is:','["Permanent", "Very expensive", "Low in cost and easy to replace", "Blocking light"]'::jsonb,2,'Film is economical.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.B',4,'A double-layer film with air between layers improves:','["Cost", "Color", "Weight", "Insulation"]'::jsonb,3,'The air gap reduces heat loss.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.C',3,'Which is a cost of building a greenhouse?','["Materials, labor, and utilities", "Plant names", "Weather only", "Garden gnomes"]'::jsonb,0,'Construction includes many expenses.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.C',4,'A grower comparing two greenhouse plans should weigh:','["Name only", "Initial cost against long-term operating cost", "Weather only", "Color only"]'::jsonb,1,'Both costs matter.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.D',3,'When choosing a greenhouse site, growers consider:','["Street name", "Neighbor''s car", "Sun exposure, water access, and drainage", "Fence color"]'::jsonb,2,'Site factors affect success.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.D',4,'A site that floods easily is poor for a greenhouse because it:','["Helps growth", "Saves money", "Gives more light", "Causes drainage and structural problems"]'::jsonb,3,'Drainage is essential.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.E',3,'A cold frame is used to:','["Protect plants using sunlight and a transparent lid", "Freeze plants", "Heat with gas", "Store tools"]'::jsonb,0,'Cold frames harden off seedlings.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.E',4,'A hoop house differs from a heated greenhouse because it usually:','["Has no covering", "Has little or no heating", "Is underground", "Is always heated"]'::jsonb,1,'Hoop houses extend seasons simply.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.F',3,'A potting area in a greenhouse layout should be:','["Outdoors only", "Far from everything", "Close to storage and propagation", "In the boiler room"]'::jsonb,2,'Efficient workflow saves time.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.F',4,'Receiving and shipping areas should have:','["A locked wall", "No door", "No space", "Easy access for trucks and loading"]'::jsonb,3,'Logistics require access.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.G',3,'Greenhouse concepts can be applied to:','["Controlled-environment plant production", "Roads", "Wild forests", "Open-field grazing"]'::jsonb,0,'CEA uses controlled conditions.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.G',4,'Controlled-environment agriculture manages:','["Only rainfall", "Light, temperature, and humidity", "Only birds", "Only wind"]'::jsonb,1,'Growers control factors.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.H',3,'A passive greenhouse relies mainly on:','["Pumps", "Large heaters", "Natural sunlight and vents", "Complex computers"]'::jsonb,2,'Passive systems use natural processes.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.H',4,'A controlled greenhouse differs from a passive one by using:','["Only shade", "Only open doors", "No equipment", "Automated heating, cooling, and ventilation"]'::jsonb,3,'Controlled houses use equipment.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.I',3,'An agency that regulates pesticide use in greenhouses is the:','["Environmental Protection Agency", "Library board", "Department of Motor Vehicles", "Postal Service"]'::jsonb,0,'EPA oversees pesticide registration.','original'),
('127.55.d.5.I',4,'Greenhouse operators must comply with regulations to:','["Avoid customers", "Protect workers, consumers, and the environment", "Lose crops", "Raise prices"]'::jsonb,1,'Regulations ensure safety.','original'),
('127.55.d.6.A',3,'Which environmental factors are controlled in a greenhouse?','["Moon phase", "Rainfall in the field", "Temperature, light, and humidity", "Sunrise time"]'::jsonb,2,'Growers adjust conditions inside.','original'),
